---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { claims, builds, sources, validations } from "../lib/knowledge";
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
---
<Layout title="Reproducibility workspace" description="Inspect provenance-aware validation records and draft a bounded, authorized validation proposal without executing code.">
  <div class="page-container workspace"><header class="page-header"><h1>Reproducibility ledger & proposal</h1><p>Author-reported validation is not independent reproduction. This page records bounded claims and prepares reviewable data only. It does not execute a driver, download a sample, conduct research, publish a claim, or change claim state.</p></header>
    <section class="panel"><h2>Published validation ledger</h2>{validations.length ? <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table">
      <caption>Reported research contracts are distinct from directly observed Observatory results.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Validation and claim</th><th scope="col">Performer / authority</th><th scope="col">Activity / status</th><th scope="col">Build and execution scope</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{validations.map((item) => <tr id={`validation-${item.id}`}>
        <td><strong>{item.title}</strong><br/><code>{item.id}</code>{item.claimIds.map((id) => <div><a href={withBase(`/claims/${id}`)}>{claims.find((claim) => claim.id === id)?.statement ?? id}</a></div>)}</td>
        <td>{item.performedBy} / {item.authority}{item.authority === "reported" && <p>Source author reported; NOT independent Observatory reproduction.</p>}</td>
        <td>{item.activity} / {item.status}</td>
        <td>{item.buildId ? <a href={withBase(`/builds/${item.buildId}`)}>{builds.find((build) => build.id === item.buildId)?.label ?? item.buildId}</a> : "Unidentified build (cannot establish selected-build result)"}
          <p>{item.executedAt ?? "Execution date unknown"}; {item.bounds}</p>
          <details><summary>Validation contract and limits</summary><dl>
            <dt>Environment</dt><dd>{item.environment}</dd><dt>Tools and versions</dt><dd>{item.tools}</dd>
            <dt>Inputs</dt><dd>{item.inputs}</dd><dt>Expected behavior</dt><dd>{item.expected}</dd>
            <dt>{item.authority === "observed" ? "Observed result" : "Author-reported result"}</dt><dd>{item.observed}</dd>
            <dt>Authorization</dt><dd>{item.authorized ? "Recorded for the described activity" : "Not established by this record"}</dd>
          </dl><ul>{item.limitations.map((limit) => <li>{limit}</li>)}</ul>
          <p>Sources: {item.sourceIds.map((id) => <a href={withBase(`/sources/${id}`)}>{sources.find((source) => source.id === id)?.title ?? id}</a>)}</p></details>
        </td>
      </tr>)}</tbody>
    </table></div> : <p>No validation contracts published. An upstream statement is not an Observatory execution.</p>}</section>
    <section class="panel"><h2>Prepare a validation proposal</h2><p>Record only work already performed with authorization, or clearly attribute an author-reported result. This form writes a local JSON download for maintainer review; no observation is made by submitting it. Every execution field must describe the actual bounded contract, not a planned or fabricated result.</p>
      <form id="validation-form" novalidate>
        <div class="workspace-fields"><label>Validation title <input name="title" required maxlength="240" autocomplete="off" /></label><label>Linked claim IDs <select name="claimIds" multiple required size="7">{claims.map((claim) => <option value={claim.id}>{claim.id} · {claim.statement}</option>)}</select><small>Ctrl/Cmd+click to select multiple claims. At least one is required.</small></label><label>Identified build / sample <select name="buildId"><option value="">Unknown / no identified build</option>{builds.map((build) => <option value={build.id}>{build.label} ({build.id})</option>)}</select></label><label>Performer <select name="performedBy" required><option value="">Select the actual performer</option><option value="source-author">Source author</option><option value="independent-researcher">Independent researcher</option><option value="observatory">Observatory</option></select></label><label>Authority <select name="authority" required><option value="">Select claim of authority</option><option value="reported">Reported by source; not independently observed here</option><option value="observed">Directly observed by named performer</option></select></label><label>Review activity <select name="activity" required><option value="">Select actual activity</option><option value="source-inspected">Source inspected</option><option value="artifact-inspected">Artifact inspected</option><option value="behavior-reproduced">Behavior reproduced</option></select></label><label>Outcome <select name="status" required><option value="">Select actual outcome</option><option value="reported">Source-reported, not independently confirmed</option><option value="pass">Pass within bounded contract</option><option value="fail">Fail within bounded contract</option><option value="inconclusive">Inconclusive</option></select></label><label>Executed on (leave blank if no execution established) <input type="date" name="executedAt" /></label><label>Source IDs <select name="sourceIds" multiple size="6">{sources.map((source) => <option value={source.id}>{source.id} · {source.title}</option>)}</select><small>Required for source-reported activity; select exact source revisions.</small></label></div>
        <div class="workspace-fields"><label>Environment: OS, isolation, configuration and tool versions <textarea name="environment" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Tools and versions <textarea name="tools" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Inputs: actual artifact identity / hash and controlled stimuli <textarea name="inputs" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Expected observable behavior <textarea name="expected" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Observed behavior / negative result, not planned output <textarea name="observed" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Bounds and acceptance criteria <textarea name="bounds" required rows="3"></textarea></label><label>Limitations (one per line) <textarea name="limitations" required rows="3"></textarea></label></div>
        <label class="authorization"><input type="checkbox" name="authorized" /> I attest the actual described lab work was authorized. Checking this box without execution does not make the result observed or reproduced.</label>
        <p id="validation-errors" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="submit" class="button">Validate and prepare JSON</button> <button type="button" id="validation-download" disabled>Download validated proposal</button> <button type="button" id="validation-copy" disabled>Copy validated JSON</button>
      </form>
      <p id="validation-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><h3>Import and claim linking</h3><ol><li>Download the validated <code>KnowledgeProposal</code> JSON after reviewing every field. A local browser draft is not a published validation.</li><li>At the repository root, run <code>npm run import -- path/to/validation-proposal.json</code>. The importer checks the full merged catalog and refuses duplicate IDs; use <code>--replace</code> only when intentionally replacing an existing ID after reviewing the diff.</li><li>Review and commit <code>src/data/knowledge/validations/&lt;id&gt;.json</code> and add the validation ID to each linked claim’s <code>validationIds</code> in <code>src/data/knowledge/claims.json</code> when appropriate. A validation does not itself advance <code>review</code> or <code>state</code>; change those only through separately supported, reviewed evidence. Run repository validation and inspect affected claim/build/workspace pages before publishing.</li></ol>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script>import "../scripts/workspace.ts";</script>
</Layout>
<style>.workspace{padding-block:2rem 5rem}.workspace .panel{margin:1rem 0;padding:1rem 1.25rem}.workspace-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,22rem),1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1rem 0}.workspace label{display:grid;gap:.3rem}.workspace label.authorization{display:flex;align-items:start}.workspace input:not([type=checkbox]),.workspace select,.workspace textarea{width:100%;padding:.55rem;color:inherit;background:transparent;border:1px solid currentColor}.workspace small{display:block}.workspace td{vertical-align:top}.workspace td p{margin:.3rem 0}.workspace button{margin:.5rem .5rem .5rem 0}.workspace #validation-errors:not(:empty){border-left:3px solid currentColor;padding:.6rem}.workspace code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>
